Rice Processing Mills in Pakistan

Rice Processing Mills in Pakistan are an essential part of the country's rice supply chain. Their role goes beyond simply removing the husk from paddy. Modern processing facilities are designed to improve the appearance, cleanliness, consistency, and overall marketability of rice.

A typical processing operation may include:

Paddy cleaning and preparation
Drying and moisture control
Husking and separation
Rice grading
Polishing and whitening
Broken rice separation
Color and quality sorting
Final inspection
Packaging and storage

Modern processing technology can help mills achieve better consistency and reduce product losses. Proper storage is equally important because rice must be protected from excessive moisture, pests, and other conditions that can affect quality.

